== 2. THE MUTATION-PROOF: MUT-NT2's fault re-run against the drained build ==
# MUT-NT2 (gen_mut_step2b.md) is the retained starvation catch: irq_external withheld from the DUT while the driver
# holds it. Its retained catch fired the END-OF-RUN rule at record age 10. With the drain the same fault ages past
# the 17-record bound and the IN-RUN rule fires instead, so the catch survives and ITS MESSAGE CHANGES.
root: ABLATION, the landing sources with no fault, seed 3, lockstep_irq_storm
  root's own identity: 3d8e81ccd20737c7 before the fault was applied (the same sources as the landing build)
  simulation verdict: PASS
  irq_entry errors: 0
  | drain: 17 records in 104 cycles (bound 17 records, cap 193 cycles from the effective bus maxima i 3/4 d 3/4)

root: MUT-NT2 re-run, seed 3, lockstep_irq_storm
  base identity: c1189fdc15a85844      root's own identity: 3d8e81ccd20737c7
  mutation: gen_tb_top.sv, irq_external withheld from the DUT once 3572 records have retired, the driver holding it
    baseline sha256 first 16: 736a8d8099339024
    mutated  sha256 first 16: 84524c5d5e90222c
  simulation verdict: FAIL
  the run's own error line:
  | irq_entry] lines 00004 raised at cycle 22574 (order 3700) not taken within 17 records (now order 3718, mie 7fff0888 mstatus 00000088)
  | drain: 17 records in 103 cycles (bound 17 records, cap 193 cycles from the effective bus maxima i 3/4 d 3/4)
  THE MESSAGE CHANGE IS THE POINT: the retained catch read "still held and enabled at the end of the run, never
  taken"; the same fault now reads "not taken within 17 records", the in-run wording, on the same line, the same
  raise cycle 22574 and the same order 3700. The drain carried the run to order 3718, so the bound expired and the
  in-run rule judged it.

== 3. BLAST RADIUS: the drain lengthens every run's tail, so a spread of other rows was re-run ==
   lockstep_zc          PASS   17 records in 110 cycles
   ut_witness           PASS   17 records in 32 cycles
   boot_zc              PASS   17 records in 115 cycles
   lockstep_zcmp        PASS   17 records in 117 cycles
   ut_isa_cov_zc        PASS   17 records in 34 cycles
   lockstep_irq_storm   PASS   17 records in 157 cycles
   Every drain completed on RECORDS, none on the cycle cap; the busiest row used 157 cycles of the 193 the
   effective config allows, so the margin is doing real work rather than hiding a cap hit.

== 4. THE CAP AND ITS DERIVATION ==
   The cap is COMPUTED AT RUN TIME by gen_irq_drain_cap_cycles (gen_tb_pkg.sv, below the generated region) from the
   effective gen_bus_cfg of both buses after their clamps, because the four gen_{i,d}bus_{gnt,rvalid}_max plusargs
   overwrite the regime windows with only a lower clamp: a constant from the defaults would be wrong for any run
   that widens one. Formula: max over the two buses of (gnt_max + rvalid_max), plus
   GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_RECORD_OVERHEAD_CYCLES = 2 for the pipeline's own stages, times GEN_IRQ_ENTRY_BOUND_RECORDS = 17,
   plus GEN_IRQ_DRAIN_MARGIN_CYCLES = 40 for the finish handshake and the last write-back. At the regime defaults
   the runs above report i 3/4 and d 3/4, so (4+3+2)*17+40 = 193.

== 5. WHAT THIS LANDING DOES NOT ESTABLISH ==
   A line starved while the core retires NOTHING is still not judged: the drain's cap ends such a run and the
   expectation is reported open. Judging it needs a cap-rule (fail at the cap when no record retired during the
   drain) with its own red from a fault that stalls retirement, which this landing does not carry. The residual is
   therefore OWED, not closed.
